    "chunk_text": "I must also say that we have to bring former projects into operation again with the assistance of multilateral agencies, the World Bank and the ADB. One is the Climate Resilient Infrastructure Project, which was a big programme the World Bank, the ADB and various other bilateral donors also put money into to carry on various disaster resilient infrastructure programmes. That had been discontinued and it has to be put back on wheels so that we can have substantial funds flowing into that.\n\nthe local level. So, why can we not do it at the top level? That is what matters when it comes to international assistance. So, do that even if it is late, but it is not too late. The fact is, when a disaster happens, the delay in every day matters because the attention of the international community could turn on to different areas. We know that already the Ukraine issue and the Gaza issue are there. So, the attention of the Middle East and Europe is already focused elsewhere. Therefore, we need to get our closer neighbours to lead the effort to call for a donor conference. I hope it would be expedited so that enough funds would flow in."
