    "chunk_text": "the local level. So, why can we not do it at the top level? That is what matters when it comes to international assistance. So, do that even if it is late, but it is not too late. The fact is, when a disaster happens, the delay in every day matters because the attention of the international community could turn on to different areas. We know that already the Ukraine issue and the Gaza issue are there. So, the attention of the Middle East and Europe is already focused elsewhere. Therefore, we need to get our closer neighbours to lead the effort to call for a donor conference. I hope it would be expedited so that enough funds would flow in.\n\nThe other issue is about the buffer zones. When it comes to rivers, particularly major rivers like the Mahaweli and its tributaries, we need to have a proper buffer zone identified with the assistance of the NBRI, the UDA, the DMC, the Irrigation Department, the Mahaweli Authority and the SLLRDC. We will have to bring all those agencies together and decide on the buffer zone so that we would ultimately be able to determine which houses could remain there, the residents of which houses have to be shifted or relocated, which houses could be repaired and ultimately, what the buffer zone would be as far as the policy is concerned. The buffer zone would differ from place to place because of its geographic location, the height and in low-tide areas. So, these matters have to be given complete attention. I must again thank former MP, Hon. M.S. Naleem and various others who had assisted us with heavy machinery in attending to these matters."
