    "chunk_text": "The other issue is about the buffer zones. When it comes to rivers, particularly major rivers like the Mahaweli and its tributaries, we need to have a proper buffer zone identified with the assistance of the NBRI, the UDA, the DMC, the Irrigation Department, the Mahaweli Authority and the SLLRDC. We will have to bring all those agencies together and decide on the buffer zone so that we would ultimately be able to determine which houses could remain there, the residents of which houses have to be shifted or relocated, which houses could be repaired and ultimately, what the buffer zone would be as far as the policy is concerned. The buffer zone would differ from place to place because of its geographic location, the height and in low-tide areas. So, these matters have to be given complete attention. I must again thank former MP, Hon. M.S. Naleem and various others who had assisted us with heavy machinery in attending to these matters.\n\n3143 3144\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dd2\u0da5 \u0dba\u0dc0\u0dd4\u0dc6\u0dda \u0dc4\u0d9a\u0dd3\u0db8\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2025 \u0dda\u0daf\u0dca\u200d\u0dca\u0dd0\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0db1\u0dbb\u0dca 19\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0daf\u0dba \u0da2\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dd9\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Speaker) Hon. Rauff Hakeem, your time is up. \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd2\u0da5 \u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dd4\u0dc6\u0db1 \u0dc4\u0d9a\u0dd3\u0db8\u0dca \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bb0\u0ba3\u0bbf \u0bb0\u0b8a\u0baa\u0bcd \u0bb9\u0b95\u0bc0\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. Rauff Hakeem, Attorney-at-Law) Sir, the Hon. Prime Minister, who is also the Minister of Education, Higher Education and Vocational Education, is here. As far as schools are concerned, 140 schools had been impacted in Kandy alone and a few have to be relocated. Therefore, a proper needs assessment has to be done very fast. Also, make sure that you consult the local school communities - the school development societies, past pupils' associations and various others - so that you would not take a decision that would finally not be accepted by them. So, that consultation has to be held without delay. The Hon. President is expected to come to Kandy again and I hope the Hon. Prime Minister, too, would find some time to come and listen to our problems and try to give some solutions."
