    "chunk_text": "Main objective and strategies\n\n\u25cf Maximizing the renewable energy potential:\n\n\u25cf Increasing the generation of renewable\n\nenergy from 35 per cent to 70 per cent by the year 2030.\n\n\u25cf Taking the initiative to take the country\n\n\u25cf Enhancing climate resilience through\n\nnature-based solutions and financial protection.\n\n\u25cf Green Financing:\n\n\u25cf Launching the National Climate Finance Strategy 2025-2030 and providing for the financing framework necessary for implementing the climate policies.\n\n\u25cf Mobilizing resources through financial\n\ninstruments such as Green Bonds, Disaster Risk Insurance and Carbon Markets.\n\n\u25cf Generation of Green Jobs:\n\n\u25cf Giving priority to generation of green\n\njobs for the purpose of optimizing the benefits of sustainable and climatically safe transition.\n\nThe Action Plan for implementing the Nationally Determined Contributions - NDCs - of Sri Lanka (2021-2030) and Carbon Net Zero 2050 also operate in combination with this broad Climate Prosperity Vision.\n\nAt present;\n\n1. The draft of the updated Climate\n\nProsperity Plan has been finalized by now and the validation workshop was conducted on 10th October.\n\n2. Cabinet Approval is expected to be\n\nsought after obtaining the concurrence of the line Ministries relevant for the implementation of the Plan concerned.\n\n3. Projects have been identified for each of\n\nthe sectors in the Climate Prosperity Plan together with the institutions from which support can be obtained for the projects. After submitting the project proposals to the relevant parties, Sri Lanka will be able to obtain financial support from the institutions concerned for implementing the projects. 4. The Vulnerable Group of Twenty (V20),"
