    "md5": "d2348e1d00dcb5651df6d6538931e8a7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1854,
    "chunk_text": "service and was one of the finest gentlemen who served this House. I had many interesting engagements with him. Particularly, when he rose from his official chair to advise the Chair on many matters, he had occasionally - several times - shared interesting anecdotes with me about the happenings in the House in the past and what would happen in the future.\n\nSir, I am quite conscious that, as the opening speaker for the Opposition at today's Debate on this important Amendment to the Colombo Port City Economic Commission Act, I am expected to properly dissect the provisions that are to be debated today. Before I come to that, I would like to digress for a moment to speak about the recent disaster caused by Cyclone \"Ditwah\". In its aftermath, several neighbouring countries such as India, Pakistan and several others sent their Rapid Deployment Forces to this country to assist us. Among that lot, I must remember with gratitude the service of the Search and Rescue Team from the United Arab Emirates because we had the opportunity of watching what an expert and efficient service they rendered to the people of Sri Lanka. I had the privilege of seeing them work in areas such as Deltota. Deltota and Galaha areas were totally cut off from the rest of the country due to the severe and massive landslides occurred everywhere. So, we were unable to reach Deltota for almost a week and that team came there and assisted us in the search and rescue mission with such efficiency. We also remember Mr. Muneer Sadhiq, Member of the Pathahewaheta Pradeshiya Sabha representing the Samagi Jana Balawegaya, who coordinated their visit. They came there, had meetings at the Divisional Secretariat, went all over the place and assisted in the rescue missions as well as in providing dry rations and various other assistance to the affected people of the area."
