    "chunk_text": "\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc5, \u0dc0\u0dd2 \u0dc1\u0dbb\u0dc2 \u0dba\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0db8 \u0d86\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dd2\u0d9a\u0dba \u0d9c\u0dd0\u0dcf \u0d85\u0dc0\u0db0\u0dca\u200d \u0dcf\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dca\u0d9a\u0dba\u0dc0\u0dcf, \u0d86\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dd2\u0d9a\u0dba \u0d9c\u0dd0\u0dcf \u0d8b\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0d9a\u0dbb\u0dc0\u0d9a\u0dca\u0d9a\u0dba \u0dd2 \u0db6\u0dcf \u0d85 \u0dda \u0dbb \u0da7\u0dca \u0dad\u0dcf\u0dc0 \u0dc0\u0da7\u0dad\u0dca, \u0dc0\u0dd2 \u0dda\u0dc1 \u0d86 \u0dba\u0ddd\u0dad\u0d9a\u0dba\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0da7\u0dad\u0dca, \u0dc0\u0dd2 \u0dda\u0dba\u0dba \u0dbb\u0da7\u0dc0\u0dbd \u0da2\u0dd3\u0dc0\u0dad\u0dca \u0dc0\u0dcf \u0dbd \u0d82\u0d9a\u0dd2\u0d9a\u0dba\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0da7\u0dad\u0dca \u0da2 \u0db4\u0dab\u0dd2\u0dc0\u0dd4\u0da9\u0dba \u0dc4\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0dba \u0d9a \u0dbb\u0dc0 \u0dbd\u0db6 \u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dcf \u0d85\u0dc0\u0dc1\u0dba\u0dba\u0dd2 \u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dba\u0dbd \u0db8\u0db8 \u0dc4\u0dd2\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0 .\n\nSo, in that light, the Port City owned by the Sri Lankan Government, which is 269 hectares in extent, is a great asset that is going to give us a bonus beyond the economic opportunities we have at this point in time. That is why this Amendment to this Act is very important and we have brought in the changes to strengthen the regulatory framework. The House needs to know that the regulatory framework under the previous Act was not enough for us to run an economic zone in a global context. Also, rules-based investment incentives were not there and it was very unclear to investors as to how much incentives they would get and what we would get. Basically, earlier, any investor could get 25 years, whether it be a primary investment or a secondary investment. So, it had been like that. There was no standardization across the globe as to how we would really bring these incentives in. So, therefore, this particular Amendment to the Act makes the regulations clear and gives a standard ona global context for the investors to come in. So, this is a change that is going to allow the Colombo Port City Economic Commission to approve more and more investments in the pipeline, which they were unable to do, probably, during last year.\n\nIf you take the other change that are going to take place, one is offshore banking, which is going to get regulated properly by the Central Bank. It is being clearly articulated. Then, the Personal Income Tax is going to be equitable. Otherwise, the people who work within the zone would be tax-free while those working outside"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-01-07-2026-01-07",
    "num": "2026-01-07",
    "date_str": "2026-01-07",
    "description": "Hansard of 2026-01-07",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/23112_english_2026-01-07.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-01-07-2026-01-07-0088",
    "chunk_index": 88,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "a1de3fd9364964ab715d5a9b029d0f05",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1940,
    "chunk_text": "If you take the other change that are going to take place, one is offshore banking, which is going to get regulated properly by the Central Bank. It is being clearly articulated. Then, the Personal Income Tax is going to be equitable. Otherwise, the people who work within the zone would be tax-free while those working outside\n\nIf you really look at this particular plot of land, we have 178 hectares set aside for development purposes, another 91 hectares for public utilities and also a lagoon that is going to be used for many activities.\n\nThis would be positioned as a regional business hub and the current Commission and the team are very confident that Sri Lanka would offer more opportunities beyond tax benefits based on its location and the situation in the region. IT industry, financial services, shipping and logistics, professional services and corporate headquarters, regional distribution centres and tourism would be the sectors that would attract most. We are happy to say that there has been a lot of interest shown, especially in 2025.\n\nMy Friends in the Opposition who spoke earlier have to understand that this is what the IMF said. This is exactly what Ranil Wickremesinghe agreed on with the IMF on 27th November, 2023, where he agreed to remove all the concessions. When we came into power, we had to negotiate with the IMF and come to an agreement with them on the 24 companies that had been agreed on earlier to be continued. That was the negotiation we did when the IMF said we could not even grant concessions to those 24 companies. That is how they were protected.\n\nAt the same time, the IMF clearly said that, now, we need to bring in a proper resolution, a proper Act in line with global standards for us to continue with this project. That is what this Government has done through negotiations. So, by looking at the standards and similar investments made around the world, we have brought in these changes."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-01-07-2026-01-07",
    "num": "2026-01-07",
    "date_str": "2026-01-07",
    "description": "Hansard of 2026-01-07",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/23112_english_2026-01-07.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-01-07-2026-01-07-0089",
    "chunk_index": 89,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "c62f698bec09bd6f10d002029d1bb3e7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2019,
    "chunk_text": "At the same time, the IMF clearly said that, now, we need to bring in a proper resolution, a proper Act in line with global standards for us to continue with this project. That is what this Government has done through negotiations. So, by looking at the standards and similar investments made around the world, we have brought in these changes.\n\nWe also need to understand that we are within the IMF framework and are adhering to its certain guidelines and rules. Actually, the sovereignty in taking financial decisions had been killed by you all. That is how you governed this country for the last 20 years and the Sri Lankan Government did not get enough tax revenue. So, you continued to borrow locally. Then, you went for ISBs. You got Sri Lanka into trouble, where we had to pay US Dollars 4.4 billion in external payments by 2019. That is how the crisis occurred. Now, we have\n\n339 340\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0da0\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0d82\u0d9c \u0d85 .\u0dc3\u0dd2\u0d82\u0dc4 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dc0 ]\n\n2026 \u0dad\u0dcf\u0dc0 \u0dbb\u0dd2 07\n\nrestructured that. We had a restructuring programme when this Government came into power and we agreed to it. Now, we can gradually start repaying our debt, which, again, will go up 2032 and by 2028, we only have to pay an additional Rs. 700 million. So, there is nothing to be scared about. We are on the right trajectory now.\n\nNow, this particular framework, this particular change is going to give us a bonus. What is that bonus? Today, I got this data from the team itself. With these changes and Amendments, currently, there are investments in the pipeline worth of Rs. 3.9 billion for the Colombo Port City. That is what we, as citizens, as the Opposition and as the Government of Sri Lanka, we need to be happy about. There is a funnel of Rs. 3.9 billion. And, out of that, Rs. 1.4 billion is already approved. So, it is only a matter of time until they bring in the money this year and commence those four large projects, which are worth of Rs. 1.2 billion. The applications for these projects amount to US Dollars 732,000 million."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-01-07-2026-01-07",
    "num": "2026-01-07",
    "date_str": "2026-01-07",
    "description": "Hansard of 2026-01-07",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/23112_english_2026-01-07.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-01-07-2026-01-07-0090",
    "chunk_index": 90,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "1624e7a1cf1e0ada119c847778623cae",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1923,
    "chunk_text": "Now, this particular framework, this particular change is going to give us a bonus. What is that bonus? Today, I got this data from the team itself. With these changes and Amendments, currently, there are investments in the pipeline worth of Rs. 3.9 billion for the Colombo Port City. That is what we, as citizens, as the Opposition and as the Government of Sri Lanka, we need to be happy about. There is a funnel of Rs. 3.9 billion. And, out of that, Rs. 1.4 billion is already approved. So, it is only a matter of time until they bring in the money this year and commence those four large projects, which are worth of Rs. 1.2 billion. The applications for these projects amount to US Dollars 732,000 million.\n\nWe are on a very strong growth trajectory and if you really look at the growth forecast for the country next year, the nominal growth is projected at 8.5 per cent, which was in the original plan. But, we all need to know that there is a requirement for us to keep the inflation at 5 per cent; that is a requirement under the programme because for a growing country to sustain a healthy inflation is required. The real GDP growth is planned to be at 3 per cent. That is the expectation of the IMF. With that, we are going to get a Government revenue of 15.4 per cent of GDP, which will allow us to keep bringing down our debt servicing cost. The debt servicing team who looks at debt sustainability today have projected that by 2030, the interest bill of the Government will fall from 52 per cent to 35 per cent, which, again, is going to give us a huge cushion, allowing us to invest in health and education. So, this is the trajectory we are going on. So, as a citizen, as a Parliamentarian and as a member of the Government, I urge the Opposition not to have unnecessary discussions, create false information and engage in the fearmongering campaign you carried out before the elections. Do not do it in 2026."
  },
