    "description": "Hansard of 2026-01-07",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/23112_english_2026-01-07.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-01-07-2026-01-07-0202",
    "chunk_index": 202,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "7be480d0775a33877a6fd07b9c3162e9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1785,
    "chunk_text": "With the present Amendment, whatever directives issued would be in terms of the international banking standards. International banking standards are very fluid and there is no proper definition. So, there is greater ambiguity. Therefore, I propose that an amendment be made to make the international banking standards practicable as far as possible, thereby giving the Governing Board of the Central Bank to take decisions in the interest of our banking system with regard to minimum capital adequacy.\n\nSir, now, I would like to bring some other matters to your notice. We talk about foreign investments coming in and the Sri Lankans investing especially in the real estate\n\n413 414\n\n\u0db4 \u0dbb\u0dca\u0dca \u0da2\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\nsector need about 21 approvals. Other than the UDA and a few other authorities, the Department of Wildlife Conservation, the Department of Forest Conservation and the Department of Coast Conservation are hesitant to grant approval or that process takes hell of a long time, thereby creating major problems. Therefore, I say that there should be a one-stop shop. You are talking about FDIs coming in, but, first, we should prevent the Sri Lankans who are getting frustrated and going to invest in Dubai. They are leaving Sri Lanka and going to all parts of the world to invest. So, first, please create a platform where Sri Lankans could easily invest in Sri Lanka and get substantial returns. Sir, if a real estate company in Sri Lanka sells a property, 35 per cent of that goes for taxes. At this point in time, this Government survives on the revenue collected from Income Tax, the Excise Department and the Sri Lanka Customs. So, please make available a fair and equitable process where Sri Lankans could invest in Sri Lanka because they are getting frustrated."
  },
