    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "414b8beba7f2d1c46e4b44c088318ecc",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1432,
    "chunk_text": "sector need about 21 approvals. Other than the UDA and a few other authorities, the Department of Wildlife Conservation, the Department of Forest Conservation and the Department of Coast Conservation are hesitant to grant approval or that process takes hell of a long time, thereby creating major problems. Therefore, I say that there should be a one-stop shop. You are talking about FDIs coming in, but, first, we should prevent the Sri Lankans who are getting frustrated and going to invest in Dubai. They are leaving Sri Lanka and going to all parts of the world to invest. So, first, please create a platform where Sri Lankans could easily invest in Sri Lanka and get substantial returns. Sir, if a real estate company in Sri Lanka sells a property, 35 per cent of that goes for taxes. At this point in time, this Government survives on the revenue collected from Income Tax, the Excise Department and the Sri Lanka Customs. So, please make available a fair and equitable process where Sri Lankans could invest in Sri Lanka because they are getting frustrated.\n\nToday, the BoI has become a white elephant. I believe you have brought in some amendments to the Strategic Development Projects Act. And also, please do not be dictated by the IMF. Sri Lanka has suffered a massive disaster. Also, we need to give tax concessions. If you take our region, Sri Lanka is not competitive with our energy costs and labour costs being high."
