    "md5": "3b2a96a5aba17e80204f5455c07f096d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2022,
    "chunk_text": "\uf0b7 In this regard, a well-defined and credible inflation target helps reduce the erosion of domestic savings by serving as an anchor for price stability. When the target is clearly communicated and consistently pursued, it helps shape public and market expectations about future inflation.\n\n\uf0b7 The Central Bank and the Government maintain a coherent macroeconomic policy framework, anchored by prudent monetary policy, fiscal consolidation and a market-determined, flexible exchange rate. These policies have helped anchor inflation expectations, rebuild investor confidence and strengthen macroeconomic stability. For long-term foreign direct investment, this environment offers both stability and growth potential.\n\n7. \uf0b7 According to Section 26(4) of the Central Bank Act, \"The Minister and the Central Bank may review the inflation target and any other parameters relating thereto once in every three years or in such other intervals, if exceptional circumstances so warranted.\" Accordingly, the current inflation target, which was set out in October, 2023, remains in effect for a three-year period. So, in future, if needed, we can consider adjusting it.\n\n8. \uf0b7 No. Inflation being targeted at 5 per cent is appropriate.\n\n\uf0b7 Meanwhile, a flexible exchange rate will allow timely adjustment to the exchange rate in line with the fundamentals and external shocks, thus helping to maintain export competitiveness.\n\n\uf0b7 Greater predictability of inflation for exporters will help their business planning and investment process.\n\n9 \uf0b7 Under the International Monetary Fund Extended Fund Facility - IMF-EFF - Programme, the Monetary Policy Consultation Clause - MPCC - has been introduced to monitor monetary policy performance in line with the domestic price stability objective.\n\n487 488\n\n\u0db4\u0db1 \u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dd2\u0dda\u0daf\u0dca\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0dc0\n\n10. \uf0b7 As indicated in response to the Question No. 7 - this is connected to the Question No. 7 - the review process of the inflation target for the next three years will commence soon."
  },
