    "chunk_text": "2024 11.00 10.00 7.00 7.53 1.20\n\nIn all the years, except in the year 2022, the yield or the\n\nrate of return given by the EPF to its members had been higher.\n\n04. The Answer given in No. 02 above applies.\n\n06. (a) The Annual Report of the Fund, which\n\nincludes the financial statements, the Auditor-General\u2019s report and other relevant information, is submitted to the Ministry of Labour for subsequent presentation to Parliament.\n\n(b) Requirement of actuarial valuation does not arise since EPF is a defined benefit plan that accrues member balances based solely on earned income.\n\n07. Approval of the Cabinet of Ministers had been obtained for procuring an IT solution for EPF. Accordingly, arrangements are in place to design a comprehensive IT solution collaboratively by the Department of Labour and the Central Bank of Sri Lanka. Also note that some facilities such as online access to EPF monthly contribution payments and accounts are available in the current IT system.\n\n08. The Code of Conduct applicable to all staff of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka is published on its website. For that, refer to https://www.cbsl.gov.lk/en/about/organisational-structure/governance-codes-and-policies.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0dbb\u0dd3 \u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a \u0db8\u0db3\u0dad\u0dca\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bb0\u0bb5\u0bbf \u0b95\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95) (The Hon. Ravi Karunanayake) Hon. Deputy Minister, it is not there on the website. I am asking a specific question. I would like an answer for that, for it is being evaded all over.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 (\u0d86\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dcf \u0dba) \u0d85\u0db1\u0dd2\u0dbd\u0dca \u0da2\u0dba\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca \u0db8\u0db3\u0dad\u0dca\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0b95\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf) \u0b85\u0ba9\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0b9c\u0baf\u0ba8\u0bcd\u0ba4) (The Hon. (Dr.) Anil Jayantha) First, let me finish the Answer. Actually, the Code of Conduct is a detailed and a lengthy one. Therefore, I cannot read it out. So, that is on the website.\n\n09. No policy decision has been taken on this until now."
