    "chunk_size_bytes": 1845,
    "chunk_text": "01. A detailed Answer is given in Annex 01. I will just read out key figures. In 2026, the target is US Dollars 23.6 billion, In 2027, the target is US Dollars 28.3 billion. Likewise, it goes up to US Dollars 36 billion.\n\n03. The impact of the newly imposed Trump tariff on Sri Lanka\u2019s export earnings would be the net effect of the behaviour of market forces in all the countries in the medium to long-term. The Government of Sri Lanka has made successful bilateral negotiations to reduce the increased tariff and further, proceedings are underway towards bringing a positive impact on the country. Overall, the impact will be dependent upon the conclusion of tariff negotiations by other countries, particularly the ones in the region.\n\n04. With the view to facilitate the export target of the Government, all possibilities are being explored to access new markets through the set of policy tools, including entering into new free trade or preferential trade agreements with countries in which trade creation is positive. Among the key factors of the criteria are, the market potential, possibility to enhance the already signed agreements and emerging opportunities.\n\n05. In line with the changing global dynamics, strategies are implemented to export high-value-added products to promote best use of resources.\n\n06. Again, a detailed Answer is given in Annexes 02 and 03. I can outline some of the key factors. One is, investment facilitation through the BoI and even through the recently passed Colombo Port City Economic Commission (Amendment) Bill.\n\n07. The Government supports the Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises - MSMEs - through several concessional credit schemes to enhance access to\n\nfinance, through which the export-oriented MSMEs can also meet their financing needs.\n\nAccordingly,\n\n1. the Small and medium-sized Enterprises"
