    "chunk_size_bytes": 2013,
    "chunk_text": "07. The Government supports the Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises - MSMEs - through several concessional credit schemes to enhance access to\n\nfinance, through which the export-oriented MSMEs can also meet their financing needs.\n\nAccordingly,\n\n1. the Small and medium-sized Enterprises\n\n2. For the stimulating package for re-energizing\n\nthe micro, small, and medium-sized enterprises sector in Sri Lanka - that is, the Re-MSME package - Rs. 20 billion has been allocated annually for both 2025 and 2026.\n\n3. The Agriculture Value Chain Sector Development Programme, an ADB-funded Programme for US Dollars 70 million, will commence in 2026.\n\n4. Another SME sector development programme funded by the ADB amounting to US Dollars 120 million will also commence in 2026.\n\nSo, including these SME packages and other financing packages, the Government has set aside Rs. 96 billion altogether in the Budget.\n\nTo address collateral-related challenges in conventional lending, the National Credit Guarantee Institution Limited - NCGIL - was established with ADB support and operationalized in February, 2025. During the period, NCGIL has issued 458 guarantees worth Rs. 1.7 billion for loans worth of Rs. 2.5 billion, including nine guarantees of Rs. 59 billion for export-oriented businesses.\n\n08. Upon conclusion of the facilitative regulation, it is\n\nenvisaged that approximately 2 per cent of GDP would be realized as FDIs through the BoI, the Port City and other investments to non-BoI entities as well.\n\n09. There are three incentive schemes available to\n\ninvestors:\n\n1. Under the Inland Revenue Act, No. 24 of\n\n2017\n\n2. Under the Strategic Development Projects\n\nAct, No. 14 of 2008, which is being reviewed; and\n\n3. Under the Colombo Port City Economic\n\nCommission Act, No. 11 of 2021, which was amended recently.\n\nThose incentives are rules-based rather than\n\ndiscretionary.\n\nDetails relating to these incentives are available in the respective institutions and organizations.\n\n687 688\n\n2026 \u0da2\u0db1\u0dc0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd2 09"
